IMPORT prelude

-- Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) — THE
-- NOUNS. Facts about the contract, the misrepresentation, what the insurer
-- would have done, and the claim. No rules here.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2012-6.txt (point in time
-- 12 August 2016).

§ `Nouns`

-- s 1 "consumer insurance contract"; s 12(4) commencement.
DECLARE `Contract facts` HAS
    `the policyholder is an individual`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `wholly or mainly for purposes unrelated to their trade, business or profession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer is party by way of an insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered into after the Act came into force`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Sch 1 para 9(5)
    `wholly or mainly life insurance`                   IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Misrepresentation facts` HAS
    `a misrepresentation was made`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1)-(4): the finding on reasonable care.
    `the consumer took reasonable care`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(5)
    `made dishonestly`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(2)(a): knew it untrue or misleading, or did not care; NOTHING if
    -- neither shown.
    `knew it untrue, or did not care`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(5)(a): a reasonable consumer would have known it untrue or
    -- misleading.
    `a reasonable consumer would have known it untrue`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(2)(b): knew the matter was relevant, or did not care; NOTHING if
    -- neither shown.
    `knew it relevant, or did not care`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(5)(a)-(b)
    `a reasonable consumer would have known it relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `asked a clear and specific question about it`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(1)(b), Sch 1 para 4: what the insurer would have done without the
-- misrepresentation.
DECLARE `What the insurer would have done` IS ONE OF
    `the same contract on the same terms`
    `no contract on any terms`
    `the contract, on these terms` HAS
        `different terms, other than the premium`       IS A BOOLEAN
        `the premium it would have charged`             IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Money facts` HAS
    `the premium actually charged`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the premiums paid`                                 IS A NUMBER
    -- Sch 1 para 2(b): the part of the premiums it would be unfair to keep.
    `premiums unfair to retain`                         IS A NUMBER
    -- The amount of the claim under the contract's terms, and (para 6)
    -- under the different terms.
    `the claim under the actual terms`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the claim under the different terms`               IS A NUMBER
